{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>Are they not across the Jordan</b> — ס\"ת אהרן (sum of Torah: Aaron), for until now the clouds were at his hand, showing them the way to one another, and now the clouds had ceased; therefore he needed to give them a sign to know the way. The verse begins and ends with ה\"א (five): He commanded them to do five things — ונתצתם (you shall tear down), ושברתם (you shall smash), תשרפון (you shall burn), תגדעון (you shall hew down), ואבדתם (you shall destroy). And likewise He said to them five things, to conclude: מבוא השמש (going down of the sun), בארץ הכנעני (in the land of the Canaanite), היושב בערבה (who dwells in the Arabah), מול הגלגל (opposite Gilgal), אצל אלוני מורה (by the oaks of Moreh)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:09:31.796147230Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}